.TH CAUDIO 1 "" "caudio X.Y.Z" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
caudio \- C++23 headless music player daemon and CLI
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B caudio
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
\fISUBCOMMAND\fR [\fIARGS\fR]...
.br
.B caudio
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
\fBstart\fR [\fB\-\-foreground\fR]
.br
.B caudio
\fBseek\fR \fITIME\fR
.br
.B caudio
\fBvolume\fR [\fILEVEL\fR]
.br
.B caudio
\fBqueue\fR \fISUBCOMMAND\fR
.br
.B caudio
\fBplaylist\fR \fISUBCOMMAND\fR
.br
.B caudio
\fBlibrary\fR \fISUBCOMMAND\fR
.br
.B caudio
\fBconfig\fR \fISUBCOMMAND\fR
.br
.B caudio
\fBtag\fR \fISUBCOMMAND\fR
.br
.B caudio
\fBhistory\fR \fISUBCOMMAND\fR
.br
.B caudio
\fBdevice\fR \fISUBCOMMAND\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B caudio
is a C++23 headless music player. It consists of a background daemon
(\fBcaudio start\fR) and a CLI that communicates with the daemon over a
local IPC channel (Unix Domain Socket on POSIX, Named Pipe on Windows)
using a JSON protocol with a 4\-byte big\-endian length prefix.
Audio decoding uses FFmpeg (libavformat/avcodec/avutil/swresample).
The library is split into modules: \fBcaudio::utils\fR, \fBcaudio::player\fR,
\fBcaudio::db\fR, \fBcaudio::engine\fR, plus \fBcaudio::cli\fR/\fBservice\fR/\fBclient\fR.
.PP
Shared\-memory status (\fBAtomicShmStatus\fR) is published at 10 fps for
low\-latency TUI polling without IPC round\-trips.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-\-config " \fIFILE\fR"
Config file path. Default is XDG config home on POSIX
(\fB$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/caudio/config.json\fR or \fB~/.config/caudio/config.json\fR)
and \fB%LOCALAPPDATA%/caudio/config.json\fR on Windows.
.TP
.BR \-\-log\-level " \fILEVEL\fR"
Daemon log level: \fBtrace\fR|\fBdebug\fR|\fBinfo\fR|\fBwarn\fR|\fBerror\fR.
.TP
.BR \-\-device " \fIDEVICE\fR"
Audio output device ID. Overrides config.
.TP
.BR \-\-version
Show version (\fBcaudio::versionFull\fR, e.g. \fBvX.Y.Z\fR) and exit.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print help and exit.
.TP
.BR \-\-daemon ", " \-\-foreground
Internal daemon flags. Do not pass manually; used by \fBcaudio start\fR
when spawning the background process.
.SH COMMANDS
.SS Daemon lifecycle
.TP
.B start [\-\-foreground]
Start daemon. By default spawns a background process (fork/CreateProcess
with \fBDETACHED_PROCESS\fR) and polls for socket readiness. With
\fB\-\-foreground\fR runs in the foreground (for systemd or debugging).
Creates DB parent directories if needed and derives the socket path
from the DB path via \fBcaudio::config::socketPathFor\fR.
.TP
.B shutdown
Stop daemon. Sends \fBShutdown\fR IPC command and polls for socket and
pid file removal. Reports an error if the daemon is still running.
.SS Playback control
.TP
.B play
Start playback. If paused, resumes; if playing, restarts; if stopped,
replays the stopped track (or starts from queue head when nothing was
stopped).
.TP
.B pause
Pause playback, preserving position. Warns without failing when nothing
is playing.
.TP
.B resume
Resume from paused position. Warns without failing when already playing;
plays from cursor when stopped.
.TP
.B restart
Seek to 0 and ensure playing state.
.TP
.B stop
Stop playback and clear current track. A later play replays the stopped
track.
.TP
.B next
Advance to next track. Handles \fBRepeatMode::One\fR and shuffle. At queue
end wraps to the head (reshuffling when shuffle is on), in every repeat
mode. Natural track end behaves the same except with repeat
\fBoff\fR, which stops instead of wrapping.
.TP
.B prev
Go to previous track. Warns without failing at queue start.
.TP
.B seek \fITIME\fR
Seek to position. \fITIME\fR can be absolute (\fBmm:ss\fR or seconds,
e.g. \fB1:30\fR or \fB90\fR) or relative (\fB+N\fR/\fB\-N\fR). Relative
seeks fetch current position via \fBStatusReq\fR and clamp to 0.
Prints nothing on success; errors go to stderr.
.TP
.B status [\-\-json] [\-\-watch] [\-\-follow] [\-\-interval \fIMS\fR]
Show playback status (state, position, duration, volume, shuffle,
repeat, track id/title/artist/path, queue size/index). \fB\-\-json\fR
emits JSON. \fB\-\-watch\fR/\fB\-\-follow\fR polls continuously every
\fB\-\-interval\fR ms (default 1000) with timestamps in text mode or
compact JSON per line in JSON mode.
.TP
.B volume [\fILEVEL\fR]
Get or set volume. \fILEVEL\fR: \fB0\fR\-100 (absolute), \fB+N\fR/\fB\-N\fR
(delta, clamped), \fBmute\fR/\fBunmute\fR. Absolute \fB0\fR counts as
\fBmute\fR. Muting remembers the current level; \fBunmute\fR restores it.
No argument prints current volume (\fBVolume: muted\fR when muted).
.TP
.B info [\-\-json]
Show detailed info for the currently playing track (metadata + play
statistics).
.SS Queue
.TP
.B queue list [\-\-json]
List all queues (id, name, track count, active marker). \fBqueue
queues\fR is a hidden alias.
.TP
.B queue tracks [\-\-order added|playback] [\-\-json]
List tracks in the active queue in playback order (shuffle order by
default) or insertion order (\fB\-\-order added\fR). The current track
row is marked with \fB>\fR (green on color terminals).
.TP
.B queue switch \fIQID\fR
Switch active queue by ID. Engine validates that the queue exists.
Switching resets the cursor to the head.
.TP
.B queue create \fINAME\fR
Create a new empty queue named \fINAME\fR.
.TP
.B queue delete \fIQID\fR
Delete queue \fIQID\fR. The active queue cannot be deleted.
.TP
.B queue add [\fIPATH\fR ...] [\-\-id \fIID\fR] [\-\-search] [\-\-recursive] [\-\-json]
Add files to the queue. Each \fIPATH\fR is a file, folder, or glob
(expanded client-side and sorted); missing library rows are added
automatically with metadata. \fB\-\-id\fR adds one library track by id.
\fB\-\-search\fR adds FTS matches for a single query. Already-queued
tracks warn and are skipped. Prints per-track confirmations plus a total.
\fB\-\-playlist \fIPID\fR\fR appends playlist tracks instead of paths;
with \fB\-\-replace\fR the active queue is cleared first.
.TP
.B queue remove [\fIPATH\fR ...] [\-\-id \fIID\fR] [\-\-pos \fIPOS\fR] [\-\-recursive] [\-\-json]
Remove from the active queue by file/folder/glob, library id
(\fB\-\-id\fR), or queue position (\fB\-\-pos\fR). The three selectors
are exclusive; a bare number is rejected. Prints one confirmation per
removed track.
.TP
.B queue move \fIFROM\fR \fITO\fR
Move track within queue from index \fIFROM\fR to \fITO\fR (atomic
clear+re\-enqueue transaction).
.TP
.B queue clear
Clear entire queue atomically. Playback of the current track continues.
.TP
.B queue shuffle [\fIon\fR|\fIoff\fR]
Set shuffle mode. No argument toggles. The resulting state is printed.
.TP
.B queue repeat [\fIoff\fR|\fIone\fR|\fIall\fR]
Set repeat mode (\fBall\fR maps to
\fBRepeatMode::All\fR). No argument cycles \fBoff\fR \-> \fBall\fR \->
\fBone\fR \-> \fBoff\fR and prints the new mode.
.SS Playlist
.TP
.B playlist list [\-\-json]
List all playlists.
.TP
.B playlist create \fINAME\fR
Create an empty playlist named \fINAME\fR.
.TP
.B playlist add \fIPID\fR [\-\-id \fIID\fR ...] [\fIPATH\fR ...]
Add library tracks (by id) or files (auto-added to the library) to
playlist \fIPID\fR. Re-adds warn and are skipped.
.TP
.B playlist tracks \fIPID\fR [\-\-json]
List tracks in playlist \fIPID\fR under a \fBPlaylist (N tracks):\fR header.
.TP
.B playlist load \fIPID\fR [\-\-play] [\-\-replace]
Load playlist \fIPID\fR into a new queue (playback and the current queue
stay intact). With \fB\-\-play\fR switches to the new queue and starts
playback. With \fB\-\-replace\fR overwrites the active queue instead.
.TP
.B playlist save \fINAME\fR [\-\-queue \fIQID\fR]
Save queue as a new playlist named \fINAME\fR. Optionally specify queue
ID (default active queue).
.TP
.B playlist delete \fIPID\fR
Delete playlist \fIPID\fR.
.TP
.B playlist rename \fIPID\fR \fINAME\fR
Rename playlist \fIPID\fR to \fINAME\fR.
.TP
.B playlist export \fIPID\fR \fIPATH\fR [\-\-format m3u|pls|json]
Export playlist \fIPID\fR to file \fIPATH\fR. Formats: \fBm3u\fR (default),
\fBpls\fR, \fBjson\fR.
.TP
.B playlist import \fIPATH\fR [\-\-name \fINAME\fR]
Import playlist from file \fIPATH\fR. If \fB\-\-name\fR omitted, derived
from filename. Lines are matched against the library
(separator-insensitive); unmatched lines are skipped and already-listed
tracks counted as duplicates. The report names matched, skipped, and
duplicate counts.
.SS Library
.TP
.B library scan [\-\-path \fIPATH\fR] [\-\-full\-hash] [\-\-json]
Scan library for audio files. Default path is the music directory
adjacent to the DB. Prints how many tracks were newly added.
\fB\-\-full\-hash\fR uses full-file BLAKE3 instead of the default
sampled fingerprint (slower). The two fingerprint modes are
incompatible: rescanning the same files with a different mode re-adds
them as new tracks.
.TP
.B library search \fIQUERY\fR [\-\-limit \fIN\fR] [\-\-json]
FTS5 search with \fBLIKE\fR fallback over metadata and filename.
Prints a match table with the query highlighted on color terminals.
.TP
.B library stats [\-\-most\-played \fIN\fR] [\-\-queue all|\fIQID\fR] [\-\-playlist \fIPID\fR] [\-\-json]
Show library counts (tracks/queues/playlists). With
\fB\-\-most\-played \fIN\fR\fR also shows totals and the top-N most
played (\fB0\fR for totals only). \fB\-\-queue\fR and
\fB\-\-playlist\fR append brief overviews (repeatable);
\fB\-\-json\fR takes neither.
.TP
.B library list [\-\-query \fIQ\fR] [\-\-artist \fIA\fR] [\-\-album \fIA\fR] [\-\-genre \fIG\fR] [\-\-limit \fIN\fR] [\-\-offset \fIN\fR] [\-\-json]
List library tracks with optional filtering and pagination.
.TP
.B library add \fIPATH\fR [\-\-recursive]
Add file or directory to library with metadata extraction.
.TP
.B library remove \fIID\fR
Remove track from library by ID or path. The confirmation names the
track; files on disk are untouched.
.SS Tags
.TP
.B tag edit \fIID\fR \fIFIELD\fR \fIVALUE\fR
Edit track tag. \fIFIELD\fR: \fBtitle\fR|\fBartist\fR|\fBalbum\fR|\fBalbum_artist\fR|\fBgenre\fR|\fByear\fR|\fBtrack_number\fR|\fBdisc_number\fR.
Database only: audio files on disk are untouched.
.TP
.B tag get \fIID\fR [\fIFIELD\fR] [\-\-json]
Get track tags for track \fIID\fR, or one field with \fIFIELD\fR.
.SS History
.TP
.B history list [\-\-limit \fIN\fR] [\-\-json]
List playback history. Default limit 50.
.TP
.B history clear
Clear playback history.
.SS Device
.TP
.B device list [\-\-json]
List audio output devices (via miniaudio enumeration).
.TP
.B device set \fIID\fR
Set default audio output device.
.TP
.B device test [\-\-id \fIID\fR]
Check audio device is available (enumeration only, no sound). Defaults to current config device.
.SS Config
.TP
.B config get \fIKEY\fR [\-\-json]
Get config value for \fIKEY\fR.
.TP
.B config set \fIKEY\fR \fIVALUE\fR
Set config value. \fIVALUE\fR is stored as JSON or plain string.
Prints nothing on success.
.TP
.B config list [\-\-json]
List all config key/value pairs.
.TP
.B config export \fIPATH\fR
Copy config file to \fIPATH\fR.
.TP
.B config import \fIPATH\fR
Validate \fIPATH\fR as a JSON object with correctly typed keys, then
replace the live config. Invalid files are rejected untouched.
.TP
.B config reset [\fIKEY\fR]
Reset config \fIKEY\fR or all keys to defaults.
.SS Preview
.TP
.B preview \fIFILE\fR
Ephemeral playback of \fIFILE\fR without daemon (direct \fBcaudio::player::Player\fR).
Blocks until playback finishes.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Start daemon and play a file:
.B caudio start
.br
caudio queue add ~/Music/album/track.flac
.br
caudio play
.br
caudio status
.TP
Search and queue:
.B caudio library search
                                   "beatles" --limit 10
.br
.B caudio queue add
                                   "beatles" --search
.br
.B caudio next; caudio status --json
.TP
Library scan and stats:
.B caudio library scan --path ~/Music --full-hash
.br
.B caudio library stats --most-played 10 --json
.TP
Live status polling (for scripts/TUI):
.B caudio status --watch --interval 200
.TP
Volume control:
.B caudio volume 75
.br
caudio volume +5
.br
caudio volume mute
.br
caudio volume
.TP
Playlist workflows:
.B caudio playlist save "My Mix";
caudio playlist export 1 /tmp/mix.m3u --format m3u
.br
.B caudio playlist import /tmp/
        mix.m3u --name "Imported"
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/caudio/config.json (POSIX)
.TP
.I
        %LOCALAPPDATA%\\caudio\\config.json (Windows) Default config file. Overridden by \fB\-\-
    config\fR. Stores DB path,
    socket path, device, log level,
    etc.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/caudio/caudio.db (POSIX)
.TP
.I %LOCALAPPDATA%\\caudio\\caudio.db (Windows)
Default SQLite database path. Contains tracks,
    queues, playlists, history,
    FTS5 index. Parent directories are created automatically.
.TP
.I /tmp/caudio-
            <hash>.sock (POSIX).
.TP
.I \\\\.\\pipe\\caudio-
            <hash> (Windows) IPC socket / named pipe.
Canonical path derived from DB path hash via
\fBcaudio::config::socketPathFor\fR. Hash is BLAKE3 of the DB path.
POSIX base is \fB$XDG_RUNTIME_DIR\fR, else \fB$XDG_DATA_HOME\fR, else
\fB/tmp/caudio\fR.
.TP
.I
/tmp/caudio-<hash>.pid
or %LOCALAPPDATA%/caudio/
caudio.pid Daemon pid file.
Path derived from DB path via \fBcaudio::config::pidPathFor\fR.
.TP
.I
/dev/shm/caudio-<hash> (POSIX) or
named shared memory (Windows)
SHM status block (\fBAtomicShmStatus\fR) for 10 fps TUI polling.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success (including \fBstart\fR when the daemon is already running).
.TP
.B 1
Runtime, daemon-side, or validation error.
.TP
.B 105
CLI11 option-value validation failure (e.g. bad \fB\-\-format\fR).
.TP
.B 106
Missing required argument.
.TP
.B 109
Unknown command or argument.
